    "description": "<h2>Summary</h2><p>Two Deals with the same Operator + Partner + Market Country/State + Vertical + Source must not both exist — the CMS rejects the second with <code>makeup_owned_by_other</code> (409), minutes after the save, in a webhook response nobody is watching.</p><p><code>External_Deal_ID__c</code> looks like it already guards this but can&#039;t: it is frozen at creation, so it describes the makeup the deal <em>had</em>, not the one it has.</p><p>This adds <code>Deal_Makeup_Key__c</code> — a text field carrying the Unique index, stamped on every save from the derivation the flow already computes — with a Custom Error that names the existing deal. Supersedes the Deal portion of BUILD-08.</p><h2>Current state</h2><ul><li><p><code>External_Deal_ID__c</code> is unique + external id, stamped once under an <code>IS NULL</code> entry filter and never rewritten. Correct for the CMS, which keys its copy of the deal on it — but useless as a live constraint.</p></li><li><p><code>Get_Highest_Match</code> / <code>fxNextSuffix</code> / <code>fxFinalId</code> append <code>-002/-003…</code> when a base key collides. Never fired on a surviving record. <strong>Left in place by this ticket</strong> — see step 2.</p></li><li><p>No Deal duplicate rules exist. BUILD-08 has carried the block-vs-flag question since 2026-07-04.</p></li><li><p>Two platform constraints fix the shape: a formula field <strong>cannot</strong> be marked Unique, and a before-save flow <strong>cannot</strong> read same-record formula fields. So the guard is a stamped text field fed by a flow formula.</p></li></ul><h2>Proposed solution</h2><p><strong>1. New field</strong> <code>Deal_Makeup_Key__c</code> <strong>— Text(80)</strong></p><ul><li><p>Unique: YES · Treat &quot;ABC&quot; and &quot;abc&quot; as duplicates: YES · External ID: no · Required: no</p></li><li><p>Not added to page layouts; available to reports.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Field Description</strong> (paste as-is):</p><blockquote><p>Uniqueness guard: enforces one Deal per Operator + Partner + Market Country/State + Vertical + Source, matching the CMS rule &quot;one deal per combination&quot; </p></blockquote><p><strong>Help Text:</strong> n/a — not on page layouts.</p><p><strong>2. Extend the existing before-save flow</strong> — <code>fxBaseKey</code> already computes the derivation correctly for a before-save context, so reuse it rather than writing a third copy:</p><ul><li><p>Remove the entry filter so the flow runs on every create and update.</p></li><li><p>Move the null check to a Decision before <code>Set_External_Id</code>: assign <code>External_Deal_ID__c</code> only when <code>ISBLANK({!$Record.External_Deal_ID__c})</code>. This keeps the id immutable once set, and makes clear-and-regenerate the one sanctioned way to change it — which BUILD-273 depends on.</p></li><li><p>Add an always-run assignment: <code>$Record.Deal_Makeup_Key__c = {!fxBaseKey</code>}.</p></li><li><p><strong>Leave</strong> <code>Get_Highest_Match</code><strong>,</strong> <code>fxNextSuffix</code> <strong>and</strong> <code>fxFinalId</code> <strong>exactly as they are</strong>; <code>Set_External_Id</code> keeps assigning <code>fxFinalId</code>. The suffix counter is under review and is not touched here (BUILD-276). Note what this means in practice: with the duplicate block ahead of it, the counter is unreachable — a colliding save is rejected before <code>Set_External_Id</code> runs — so this ticket leaves the code standing, not the behaviour. The accepted cost is a second SOQL query on every Deal save that will never return a row.</p></li><li><p>Relabel the flow to &quot;Deal - Before Save - Set Deal Keys&quot;; keep the API name </p></li></ul><p>Element order: Start → <code>Get_Existing_Makeup</code> → Decision <code>Duplicate_Found?</code> → (yes) Custom Error / (no) → Decision <code>External_Id_Blank?</code> → (yes) <code>Get_Highest_Match</code> → <code>Set_External_Id</code> → <code>Set_Makeup_Key</code>.</p><blockquote><p>Removing the entry filter moves the &quot;id never changes&quot; guarantee from a filter to a Decision branch — self-evident becomes needs-proving. AC 5 and 6 cover it; don&#039;t waive them.</p></blockquote><p><strong>3. Custom Error for the message, index for the control</strong></p><ul><li><p><code>Get_Existing_Makeup</code>: Get Records on <code>Deal__c</code> where <code>Deal_Makeup_Key__c</code> equals <code>{!fxBaseKey</code>} and <code>Id</code> does not equal <code>{!$Record.Id</code>}, first record only.</p></li><li><p>If found → Custom Error, record-level: <em>&quot;A deal with this Operator, Partner, Market, Vertical and Source already exists: {existing deal Name} ({existing Deal Number}). Add a Deal Rep Assignment to that deal instead of creating a new one. If the commercial terms have changed, check with the team before creating a second deal.&quot;</em></p></li></ul><p><strong>4. New field</strong> <code>Makeup_Drift__c</code> <strong>— Formula (Checkbox)</strong>, BUILD-273&#039;s completion check. Safe as a formula field: read in reports, never by the flow.</p><pre><code>NOT(ISBLANK(External_Deal_ID__c)) &amp;&amp; External_Deal_ID__c &lt;&gt; Deal_Makeup_Key__c</code></pre><p><strong>Field Description</strong> (paste as-is):</p><blockquote><p>TRUE when a Deal&#039;s frozen External Deal ID no longer matches its current makeup — the makeup changed after the ID was stamped, or the ID predates a change to the derivation.</p></blockquote><p><strong>Help Text:</strong> n/a — not on page layouts.</p><p><strong><s>5. Runbook + cross-references</s></strong> <s>—</s> <code>fxSourceCode</code> <s>must mirror</s> <code>Source_Code__c</code> <s>permanently, because a before-save flow cannot read the field. Make the coupling discoverable: reciprocal notes in the field and flow descriptions (same for</s> <code>Market_State_Code__c</code> <s>/</s> <code>fxStateCode</code><s>,</s> <code>Region_Code__c</code><s>, and the Vertical CASE that silently falls through to</s> <code>XXX</code><s>), plus an &quot;Adding a new Source value&quot; runbook section covering the Source picklist,</s> <code>Source_Code__c</code><s>,</s> <code>fxSourceCode</code><s>, WagerTech&#039;s CMS (which accepts only</s> <code>wagertech</code> <s>and</s> <code>shurzy</code> <s>today), and any Source-filtered list views. Custom Metadata is the graduation path if the list grows. → To be handled in a separate ticket</s></p><p><strong>6. Backfill</strong> — touch-save all existing Deals so every record carries a key. Genuine legacy duplicates will reject; resolve by hand and record what was found on this ticket.</p><h2>Acceptance criteria</h2><ol><li><p>Creating or editing a Deal onto an existing makeup is blocked with a message naming the existing deal. Via Data Loader, with no flow message, it still fails on the unique index.</p></li><li><p>Any one component differing — Source, Market State, Vertical — saves normally.</p></li><li><p>Test Deals are separate: one colliding only with a real deal saves; two colliding test deals are blocked.</p></li><li><p>An Inactive Deal keeps its key, so a retired combination is still blocked.</p></li><li><p><strong>External Deal ID never moves on save</strong>, including an edit that changes the makeup. On a legacy deal missing the Source suffix, the makeup key updates and the id does not.</p></li><li><p><strong>Clearing External Deal ID and saving restamps it</strong> from the current makeup.</p></li><li><p><strong>The suffix counter never fires.</strong> An attempt to create a second Deal on an existing makeup is blocked. </p></li><li><p>Blank Source still yields <code>NOSRC</code> in the id.</p></li><li><p><code>Makeup_Drift__c</code> is TRUE on a legacy suffix-less deal and FALSE on a correctly-created one. </p></li></ol><h2>Out of scope</h2><ul><li><p><strong>The</strong> <code>-002</code> <strong>suffix counter — whether to remove it, replace it with a manual version selector, or keep it and relax this ticket&#039;s dedupe rule (BUILD-276).</strong> It stays untouched here. </p></li><li><p>Consolidating <code>fxSourceCode</code> / <code>fxStateCode</code> into formula fields (not possible in before-save) or into Custom Metadata (deferred).</p></li></ul>",
