        {
          "id": "10222",
          "body": "<p><strong>Context and related tickets</strong></p><p>Drafted 2026-09-08 from the CMS Deals Webhook guide (issued 2026-09-02) plus live verification in the Partial sandbox.</p><p><strong>Why this exists:</strong> the CMS enforces one deal per Operator + Partner + Region + Vertical + Source and rejects a second with <code>makeup_owned_by_other</code> (409). Salesforce needs its own constraint so duplicates are caught at save time rather than in a webhook response minutes later.</p><p><strong>Related:</strong></p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1216276854422224/f/\">BUILD-08 — Build duplicate prevention rules: Operator, Partner, Deal</a> — supersedes its Deal scope; close once Operator/Partner rules are verified</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218294334910505/f/\">BUILD-273 — Deal: Data cleanup + regenerate Deal Names and External Deal IDs</a> — the cleanup/regeneration pass that depends on AC 6</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218291754974407/f/\">DECISION-07 — Deal versioning when commercial terms change</a> — the versioning question left open; does not block this ticket</p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218031268224540/f/\">BUILD-246 — Deal: Source_Code__c formula field (Source → shortcode)</a>, <a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218031194254612/f/\">BUILD-247 — Deal: Include Source code in External Deal ID generation</a>, <a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218031283565012/f/\">BUILD-248 — Deal: Append Source code to Deal Name automation</a>, <a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218031194314763/f/\">BUILD-249 — Deal: Require Source on record page (Dynamic Forms) + list view column</a> — the Source batch this builds on</p></li></ul><p><strong>Two things to know before starting:</strong></p><ol><li><p>The counter has never fired on a surviving record — all 28 Deals were checked, and every counter-shaped id (<code>TEST-000</code>, <code>TEST-SAMPLE-DEAL-001-099</code>) is a hand-seeded load value. The 2026-09-01 ReBet duplicate is the one likely case it did fire; that record was deleted after manual cleanup, so it is not verifiable without the Recycle Bin. No verification step is included on this ticket for that reason.</p></li><li><p>Step 5 (the Account validation rule) is a Jumpr proposal, not a client ask — cut it without affecting any acceptance criterion.</p></li></ol><p><strong>Progress field:</strong> not set at creation — it is not project-scoped on this board, so set it manually if you use it.</p>",
          "created": "2026-09-08T17:54:36.467-0400",
          "updated": "2026-09-08T17:54:36.467-0400",
          "jsdPublic": true
        },
        {
          "id": "10223",
          "body": "<p><strong>Correction to the pinned comment (2026-09-08)</strong></p><p>The pinned comment above refers to a &quot;step 5 (the Account validation rule)&quot;. That step has been <strong>removed from the description</strong> and the remaining steps renumbered — the old 6, 7 and 8 are now 5, 6 and 7. Acceptance criteria are unchanged.</p><p>Reason: <a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218294343924521/f/\">BUILD-274 — Account: Auto-generate Operator and Partner External IDs</a> generates the Operator and Partner External IDs in Salesforce, so the values feeding the Deal key are correct at the source and no downstream guard is needed. Noted under Out of scope.</p>",
          "created": "2026-09-08T18:30:57.753-0400",
          "updated": "2026-09-08T18:30:57.753-0400",
          "jsdPublic": true
        },
        {
          "id": "10224",
          "body": "<p>On Hold until we resolve decisions in this document: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KDsgXLUGtixjSIgKmW9HAGNMeoMoi1hKpBqGH4i8yBs/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.aiiwd8ktxerk\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KDsgXLUGtixjSIgKmW9HAGNMeoMoi1hKpBqGH4i8yBs/edit?tab=t.0#bookmark=id.aiiwd8ktxerk</a></p>",
          "created": "2026-09-09T12:35:15.619-0400",
          "updated": "2026-09-09T12:35:15.619-0400",
          "jsdPublic": true
        },
        {
          "id": "10225",
          "body": "<p><strong>Split 2026-09-10 — counter removal moved out, ticket un-held</strong></p><p>The External Deal ID version-suffix scope has been moved to <a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1218365315802809/f/\">BUILD-276 — Deal: External Deal ID version suffix — remove, replace, or keep</a>, pending the 2026-09-11 sync. This ticket is now the dedupe key and duplicate block only, and the title changed to match.</p><p><strong>What changed in the description:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Step 2 no longer deletes <code>Get_Highest_Match</code>, <code>fxNextSuffix</code> or <code>fxFinalId</code>. <code>Set_External_Id</code> keeps assigning <code>fxFinalId</code>, and <code>Get_Highest_Match</code> is back in the element order.</p></li><li><p>AC 7 rewritten from a removal check (&quot;no new id contains -002&quot;) to an unreachability check — the counter is still in the flow, so the test is that the duplicate block fires ahead of it and no suffixed record is produced on any path.</p></li><li><p>ACs 1–6, 8 and 9 are unchanged. Both Field Descriptions and Help Text are unchanged.</p></li><li><p><code>Region_Code__c</code> (BUILD-275) added to the step 5 cross-reference list — it is a formula field, so the before-save flow cannot read it either.</p></li><li><p>New out-of-scope entry pointing at BUILD-276.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Status moved On Hold → Up Next.</strong> The 2026-09-09 hold was pending the decisions doc; the part that was waiting is exactly the part that moved to BUILD-276, so nothing here is blocked.</p><p><strong>Worth knowing before you build:</strong> keeping the counter keeps the code, not the capability. Once the makeup key ships, <code>Get_Highest_Match</code> can never return a row — the Custom Error fires first, and the unique index catches anything that gets past it. It is a SOQL query per save that does nothing, and a code path no test can reach. Fine as a two-week holding position; not fine permanently, which is what BUILD-276 is for.</p><p><strong>Two flow versions instead of one.</strong> This split was merged back together on 2026-09-08 precisely because both halves touch the same flow and the split bought no rollback granularity. That is still true — the reason for re-splitting is that one half is now decision-blocked and a card cannot be half-blocked. If the sync lands on &quot;delete the counter&quot;, the cheapest path is to fold BUILD-276 back into this ticket before either is built and close 276 unstarted.</p><p>The pinned context comment above remains accurate and needs no edit.</p>",
          "created": "2026-09-10T10:59:20.422-0400",
          "updated": "2026-09-10T10:59:20.422-0400",
          "jsdPublic": true
        },
        {
